{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@igni/ui-react": ["./src/ui-react/index.ts"],
      "@igni/extension-bridge": ["./src/extensions/bridge.ts"],
      "@igni/ui-css": ["../ui/igni-ui.css"],
      /*
       * ``examples/`` sits outside this package, so Node resolution
       * walking up from it never reaches these. An extension author
       * has them in their own node_modules; here they have to be
       * pointed at, or the example cannot be type-checked at all.
       */
      "react": ["./node_modules/@types/react"],
      "react/*": ["./node_modules/@types/react/*"],
      "react-dom": ["./node_modules/@types/react-dom"],
      "react-dom/*": ["./node_modules/@types/react-dom/*"]
    },
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  /*
   * ``e2e`` is in here because it was not, and nothing noticed. F128.
   * Playwright transpiles each spec without type-checking it, so for as
   * long as this said ``["src"]`` the 48 e2e tests were the only
   * TypeScript in the repository that no compiler ever read — and three
   * of them do not run by default, so a type error in one of those was
   * invisible twice over.
   *
   * ``types`` is deliberately left unset: that pulls in every
   * ``@types/*`` package, which is how the specs get ``node:child_process``
   * without a second project. It also means app code can reach for
   * ``process`` — a real cost, and the reason the portal splits its
   * projects instead. Not worth the restructuring here while this
   * client's config is one flat project.
   */
  /*
   * ``../../examples`` for the same reason ``e2e`` is here, and it had
   * already happened again: the reference extension shipped with a
   * docstring claiming "this compiles", against a file no compiler had
   * ever read. It imported an alias that did not exist and a stylesheet
   * that was not there, and nothing said so.
   */
  "include": ["src", "e2e", "../../examples"]
}
